[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_vatc4")
name = "Shin"
text = "Dragon Quest is a long-running Japanese role-playing game (JRPG) franchise created in 1986 by Yuji Horii, Akira Toriyama, and Koichi Sugiyama, and published by Square Enix. Known for helping establish the console JRPG genre, the series follows heroes on fantasy quests using turn-based combat and features iconic monster designs like the blue Slime. • Creators & Style: Game designer Yuji Horii crafted the stories and systems, Dragon Ball creator Akira Toriyama designed the characters and monsters, and composer Koichi Sugiyama wrote the orchestral score.• Origins & Name Change: The first Dragon Quest game launched in Japan in 1986 on the Famicom and MSX. Early Western releases used the name Dragon Warrior due to trademark conflicts before adopting Dragon Quest globally.• Gameplay: Most mainline entries center on classic turn-based battles, party progression, town exploration, and defeating evil forces, while keeping mechanics approachable."
funfacts = Array[String](["Shin Godzilla (Shin Gojira, シン・ゴジラ) is both a 2016 Japanese kaiju film and the title monster within it, serving as Toho's third reboot of the Godzilla franchise. Co-directed by Hideaki Anno and Shinji Higuchi, the film reimagines Godzilla as a rapidly evolving, terrifying symbol of natural and nuclear catastrophe.The Film• Release & Franchise: Released in Japan on July 29, 2016, it is the 31st Godzilla film and the first entry in the franchise's Reiwa era.• Plot: A mysterious, rapidly mutating creature emerges from Tokyo Bay and rampages toward the capital. Rather than focusing solely on monster battles, much of the story follows Japanese politicians and scientists navigating slow bureaucracy to stop it.• Themes & Inspiration: Production drew heavily from the March 2011 Tōhoku earthquake, tsunami, and Fukushima nuclear disaster, as well as government crisis response.• Reception: It won major honors—including the Japan Academy Prize for Picture of the Year—and was praised for its sharp political satire and tension.", "Dragon Quest is a long-running Japanese role-playing game (JRPG) franchise created in 1986 by Yuji Horii, Akira Toriyama, and Koichi Sugiyama, and published by Square Enix. Known for helping establish the console JRPG genre, the series follows heroes on fantasy quests using turn-based combat and features iconic monster designs like the blue Slime. • Creators & Style: Game designer Yuji Horii crafted the stories and systems, Dragon Ball creator Akira Toriyama designed the characters and monsters, and composer Koichi Sugiyama wrote the orchestral score.• Origins & Name Change: The first Dragon Quest game launched in Japan in 1986 on the Famicom and MSX. Early Western releases used the name Dragon Warrior due to trademark conflicts before adopting Dragon Quest globally.• Gameplay: Most mainline entries center on classic turn-based battles, party progression, town exploration, and defeating evil forces, while keeping mechanics approachable.", "Shin Kamen Rider usually refers to a 2023 Japanese tokusatsu superhero film written and directed by Hideaki Anno to celebrate the 50th anniversary of the 1971 Kamen Rider series. It is the third entry in the Shin Japan Heroes Universe, following Shin Godzilla (2016) and Shin Ultraman (2022).Plot and Main Characters• Premise: Takeshi Hongo (Sosuke Ikematsu) is kidnapped and turned into a grasshopper-hybrid cyborg (\"Batta Augment-01\") by the secret organization SHOCKER.• Escape and Allies: Ruriko Midorikawa (Minami Hamabe), a SHOCKER member and daughter of former SHOCKER scientist Hiroshi Midorikawa, helps Hongo escape before brainwashing.• The Fight: Hongo fights SHOCKER's augmented agents as Kamen Rider and teams up with fellow cyborg Hayato Ichimonji (Tasuku Emoto), Kamen Rider No. 2.• Details: The film runs 2 hours and 1 minute with music by Taku Iwasaki.Key Themes and Style• Retro Homage: It reinterprets visuals, sound design, and storytelling elements from the original 1971 series while updating the action and character drama.• Character Conflict: The story focuses on Hongo's inner struggle between his desire to avoid violence and the aggressive instincts of his augmented body.", "Shin Ultraman is a 2022 Japanese sci-fi superhero film that reimagines the classic 1966 Ultraman TV series. Directed by Shinji Higuchi and written/co-produced by Hideaki Anno, it was co-produced by Tsuburaya Productions, Toho, and Studio Khara as part of the Shin Japan Heroes Universe.Plot & Premise• S-Class Species & SSSP: Giant unidentified monsters (\"S-Class Species\") threaten Japan, prompting the government to form the S-Class Species Suppression Protocol (SSSP) task force.• Lipiah & Kaminaga: A silver giant extraterrestrial named Lipiah arrives from space. After accidentally killing SSSP member Shinji Kaminaga during a monster battle, Lipiah fuses with and takes on Kaminaga's appearance and role to defend Earth against kaiju and hostile aliens.Key Differences & Meaning of \"Shin\"• Meaning of \"Shin\": Written in katakana (シン), the title leaves \"shin\" open to multiple interpretations—such as \"new,\" \"true,\" or \"god/divine\"—signaling a fresh, grounded take on the franchise rather than a straightforward remake. There is a consensus on Reddit that using katakana lets the title carry these overlapping meanings simultaneously.• Design Homage:"])
